// Spinner (ds-metrics §9 — Android most Loader.kt; the iOS DS has none): a static track of 7 dots (diameter 0.35 × stroke,
// `color` at 25%, on the stroke's centre line every 360°/7 from 3 o'clock — the DS's dashed ring) and a head arc of
// `color` with round caps that spins 360° every 1100 ms (autoplay timeline, forever). Stroke = size / 6.4 (5pt at the
// default 32), inside the box like the DS (centre-line radius (size − stroke) / 2). The dots are written out, not a
// repeat: a Loader may sit in a lazy list's footer, where the compiler rejects nested repeats.
// ponytail: the DS head breathes between 30° and 240° every 900 ms and tapers to 0.55 × stroke at its ends; here it is a
// fixed 135° arc (that sweep's mean) of even width — animating it needs a timeline-driven `trim`.
param size: number = 32
param color: color = @color.accentPrimary
let stroke = size / 6.4
let dot = stroke * 0.35
let r = (size - stroke) / 2
